    "created_at": "2020-09-02T06:16:43Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-09-02T06:16:43Z",
    "body": "Browsing context change should [already be possible](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#browsing-context-group-switches-due-to-cross-origin-opener-policy) with COOP right? However it looks like we're [immediately discarding](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#obtain-browsing-context-navigation) the previous BC when that happens. Not sure on the reason behind that, but I suspect we can remove the \"discard\" part to allow the previous document be preserved in bfcache. I think we can modify the \"fully active\" bit of the old browsing context there too.\r\n\r\n> Making it depend on browsing session seems reasonable.\r\n\r\nDo you mean [browsing session](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/history.html#browsing-session), or browsing context? Maybe we can have a \"fully active\" document to depend on whether the \"current history step\" (proposed in #5767) matches, hmm... (sounds more complex than just having the bit on the browser context too though)",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
